  y = 10;
} else {
  // do nothing
}
```

If `x` is always greater than 0, the condition `x > 0` is always true, and the condition `x <= 0` is never evaluated. Therefore, condition coverage is not achieved, even if statement coverage is 100%. Statement 2 is also incorrect.

